// Package {{package_name}} is an Arandu module.
//
// A module is a directory that brings its own routes, its own migrations and
// its own dependency graph. There is no container and no service discovery: the
// application constructs it by hand in bootstrap/app.go and passes it to the
// kernel.
//
//	app.Register({{package_name}}.New())
//
// [Module] is the whole public surface a host application needs. Everything it
// registers, it registers in [Module.Routes]; everything it has to prepare
// before serving goes in a Boot method, which is one of the optional interfaces
// in github.com/arandu-io/hesape/foundation.
//
// # Authorization
//
// Every path that reaches data -- writes and reads alike -- takes an
// auth.Grant and filters by auth.Tenant(g). That includes List, Find, reports
// and exports. A read path without a policy is a data leak between tenants with
// a technical name on it.
package {{package_name}}
